  "description": "NOCBIR crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C88 H70 Br8 Eu5 N12 O32 1+,N1 O3 1-,3(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Eu1 (Eu) has 9 O neighbors; Eu2 (Eu) has 7 O neighbors; Eu3 (Eu) has 4 O neighbors; Eu4 (Eu) has 7 O neighbors; Eu5 (Eu) has 9 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 4 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a chain with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.700-3.926 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 99.57-113.07°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Eu5L4(OH)2(NO3)4(H2O)2]·NO3·3H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
